r_id": "", "html_url": "https://github.com/sharkdp", "id": 4209276, "login": "sharkdp", "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjQyMDkyNzY=", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sharkdp/orgs", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sharkdp/received_events", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sharkdp/repos", "site_admin": false, "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sharkdp/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sharkdp/subscriptions", "type": "User", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/sharkdp", "user_view_type": "public"}, "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/ruff/commits/e7fb3684e83da6b74576dc3d782df5403a544177/comments", "commit": {"author": {"date": "2025-07-07T13:04:27Z", "email": "sharkdp@users.noreply.github.com", "name": "David Peter"}, "comment_count": 0, "committer": {"date": "2025-07-07T13:04:27Z", "email": "noreply@github.com", "name": "GitHub"}, "message": "[ty] Bare `ClassVar` annotations (#15768)\n\n## Summary\n\nIt was recently clarified in the [typing\nspec](https://typing.python.org/en/latest/spec/class-compat.html#classvar)\nthat bare `ClassVar` annotations are allowed. For annotated assignments\nwith a right hand side value, the spec requires type checkers to infer\nthe type as something \"to which [the] value is assignable\". For a value\nof `2`, the spec suggests `int`, `Literal[2]`, or `Any` as examples.\nHere, we choose `Unknown | Literal[2]` instead, conforming with out\nusual treatment of attribute types.\n\ncloses https://github.com/astral-sh/ty/issues/211", "tree": {"sha": "112113f34a685c160831a54b015d341a9bbf18f5", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/ruff/git/trees/112113f34a685c160831a54b015d341a9bbf18f5"}, "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/ruff/git/commits/e7fb3684e83da6b74576dc3d782df5403a544177", "verification": {"payload": "tree 112113f34a685c160831a54b015d341a9bbf18f5\nparent 4aaf32476ad470c4b42be7fb8b577ca781884151\nauthor David Peter <sharkdp@users.noreply.github.com> 1751893467 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1751893467 +0200\n\n[ty] Bare `ClassVar` annotations (#15768)\n\n## Summary\n\nIt was recently clarified in the [typing\nspec](https://typing.python.org/en/latest/spec/class-compat.html#classvar)\nthat bare `ClassVar` annotations are allowed. For annotated assignments\nwith a right hand side value, the spec requires type checkers to infer\nthe type as something \"to which [the] value is assignable\". For a value\nof `2`, the spec suggests `int`, `Literal[2]`, or `Any` as examples.\nHere, we choose `Unknown | Literal[2]` instead, conforming with out\nusual treatment of attribute types.\n\ncloses https://github.com/astral-sh/ty/issues/211", "reason": "valid", "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJoa8XbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACHQQAC3yA+V71jlZo/w/90IgmJKA\npnFx0eHACddZHbII7Wjk+vkJ0fEQU0tDVKnMyqq8v5iZJJ0qRinn9Br1eSRjv8ri\nupdTFajrIfps/TE4bynnoIssGFPu8ra5ezUYlHloJBngww/vK3vAJlFod4Uq7jd0\nrRcRk6vhXuSLxCfwrEnzQpEjS1k8O7H+joykPRO+f34zICHhAROtyn2NMFa6Muzd\nwoEO+LKoW0FoDCEzn3zUq/5jRDyiMg5+hGqy5rStkd5TpEJG4SMrElvwQzVDMhNp\nocmVS3Dxu47nGlZ/mhXpLf+WGbF7+kpXgWFlDaXwkHL/rnV0kKLz+IIFWlTxHFvg\nHGx6bYbscURbtcOPTyirRylI/I0dFbv6DytiwNN6/jsD+69MwnKlGmanKRWswnpv\nlWUo5U84+4m9pLzhEK5JLvtfnOWYzxGNyIj5+X/nahJPCoHegJGqcRozUvvXYwy/\nHyheKQ5x4r8cvPHkPOvCNwlTuX5Q1Vf4NRv2sJdegPUZlqovxPG9LRaQgYkg0mW7\nms2eV0f88GZCYGHxBBUbGyoF572BWRq9TIF97TVVLXhbR8IZ3h63cby0zwTbot3S\ncv1Y0tPPAh/yUZBuBX+7lQEBXcC/V9sUBzogRuqPIqgY2+b7E9KtndihXwBlp6he\n6UFZ3HIL/2LIgeR2vJeR\n=raH/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n", "verified": true, "verified_at": "2025-07-07T13:04:28Z"}}, "committer": {"avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}", "gravatar_id": "", "html_url": "https://github.com/web-flow", "id": 19864447, "login": "web-flow", "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos", "site_admin": false, "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions", "type": "User", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/web-flow", "user_view_type": "public"}, "html_url": "https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/e7fb3684e83da6b74576dc3d782df5403a544177", "node_id": "C_kwDOHy0BzdoAKGU3ZmIzNjg0ZTgzZGE2Yjc0NTc2ZGMzZDc4MmRmNTQwM2E1NDQxNzc", "parents": [{"html_url": "https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/4aaf32476ad470c4b42be7fb8b577ca781884151", "sha": "4aaf32476ad470c4b42be7fb8b577ca781884151", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/ruff/commits/4aaf32476ad470c4b42be7fb8b577ca781884151"}], "sha": "e7fb3684e83da6b74576dc3d782df5403a544177", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/ruff/commits/e7fb3684e83da6b74576dc3d782df5403a544177"}, {"author": {"avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4209276?v=4", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sharkdp/events{/privacy}", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sharkdp/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sharkdp/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sharkdp/gists{/gist_id}", "gravatar_id": "", "html_url": "https://github.com/sharkdp", "id": 4209276, "login": "sharkdp", "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjQyMDkyNzY=", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sharkdp/orgs", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sharkdp/received_events", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sharkdp/repos", "site_admin": false, "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sharkdp/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sharkdp/subscriptions", "type": "User", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/sharkdp", "user_view_type": "public"}, "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/ruff/commits/f76d3f87cfbfd8953087c521f36533f94f3b7304/comments", "commit": {"author": {"date": "2025-07-02T16:03:56Z", "email": "sharkdp@users.noreply.github.com", "name": "David Peter"}, "comment_count": 0, "committer": {"date": "2025-07-02T16:03:56Z", "email": "noreply@github.com", "name": "GitHub"}, "message": "[ty] Allow declared-only class-level attributes to be accessed on the class (#19071)\n\n## Summary\n\nAllow declared-only class-level attributes to be accessed on the class:\n```py\nclass C:\n    attr: int\n\nC.attr  # this is now allowed\n``` \n\ncloses https://github.com/astral-sh/ty/issues/384\ncloses https://github.com/astral-sh/ty/issues/553\n\n## Ecosystem analysis\n\n\n* We see many removed `unresolved-attribute` false-positives for code\nthat makes use of sqlalchemy, as expected (see changes for `prefect`)\n* We see many removed `call-non-callable` false-positives for uses of\n`pytest.skip` and similar, as expected\n* Most new diagnostics seem to be related to cases like the following,\nwhere we previously inferred `int` for `Derived().x`, but now we infer\n`int | None`. I think this should be a\nconflicting-declarations/bad-override error anyway? The new behavior may\neven be preferred here?\n  ```py\n  class Base:\n      x: int | None\n  \n  \n  class Derived(Base):\n      def __init__(self):\n          self.x: int = 1\n  ```", "tree": {"sha": "68564c9b4e4aa4bc723616e5c0007dd2283ed79b", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/ruff/git/trees/68564c9b4e4aa4bc723616e5c0007dd2283ed79b"}, "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/ruff/git/commits/f76d3f87cfbfd8953087c521f36533f94f3b7304", "verification": {"payload": "tree 68564c9b4e4aa4bc723616e5c0007dd2283ed79b\nparent 5f426b9f8b03688d58684da1e4ce51edcaad97dd\nauthor David Peter <sharkdp@users.noreply.github.com> 1751472236 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1751472236 +0200\n\n[ty] Allow declared-only class-level attributes to be accessed on the class (#19071)\n\n## Summary\n\nAllow declared-only class-level attributes to be accessed on the class:\n```py\nclass C:\n    attr: int\n\nC.attr  # this is now allowed\n``` \n\ncloses https://github.com/astral-sh/ty/issues/384\ncloses https://github.com/astral-sh/ty/issues/553\n\n## Ecosystem analysis\n\n\n* We see many removed `unresolved-attribute` false-positives for code\nthat makes use of sqlalchemy, as expected (see changes for `prefect`)\n* We see many removed `call-non-callable` false-positives for uses of\n`pytest.skip` and similar, as expected\n* Most new diagnostics seem to be related to cases like the following,\nwhere we previously inferred `int` for `Derived().x`, but now we infer\n`int | None`. I think this should be a\nconflicting-declarations/bad-override error anyway? The new behavior may\neven be preferred here?\n  ```py\n  class Base:\n      x: int | None\n  \n  \n  class Derived(Base):\n      def __init__(self):\n          self.x: int = 1\n  ```", "reason": "valid", "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJoZVhsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAm5wQABmlry/2kjqO+5NMdRSoJSpP\nSJ0kdrAVmKJMcPfvc90cfHvD/Fed5nSHTUM66TN4RR2JztH//IUIlE+pIILr159x\nFayN5m3lbClA7SMKNoMm4ipaiXygMgm8G5kBiE7MZ4N3A2KE6TfcyD9AbSCUNL9D\nAwiVKhEyBzMXNGtbpX6t+NZEtOtPs2UH1pJUXQvyr5wz/I3bfA9UbKksRhM8gYC6\nHXk0aiBqkiAD2UsaRKv+MtnM0E4PrqKO+c4s+T7lXaPTjFIE5mEJoA7eVDsXWSy6\nW4/qyvlrf+1oePLNBqVV6YLG1aC+bEEC2s98+vfLTx/rpOtzXODhB4EwrOwn1hCX\nnb5bEIEesTR4D3ni8/+sGPDhiyeHp+jpJlwD0z0kkOm3hh8+mxMsGLezudiwfKPe\njjaftKl3o0hSqF8J/brQHucT5rQoyP+codt3E+WYrSCJUFwCISLFs8Ysa0YYzlkP\neeRRL9ChTql2yQYCChRU/fFfQvNRxTZDkHraYiN+l+N5n5TQnIi3oEN4RwfbXFuK\nlyFqWPU4b0txhKQ42XABDhckakfQuBjXAvJVo1Jic3lt+bTS1mH0VUAHF7+OW0be\nY61sBBVV8eeV4ChuBrhC9JDB6n0ba6fEnkjEaz6PdbdpSo3PNkc